To decompose the given mission description into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we will define goals and tasks in a structured manner. The focus is on resource collection and delivery by robots, with considerations for battery management and parallel task execution.

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                     | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation   | Goal Type  | Relation |
| ------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ---------- | -------- |
| G1      | Complete Resource Mission      | Ensure all required resources are collected and delivered.           | -                    | Achieve    | -        |
| G2      | Manage Resource Collection     | Collect required resources from storage locations.                   | #                    | Perform    | G1       |
| G3      | Manage Resource Delivery       | Deliver collected resources to the specified location.               | #                    | Perform    | G1       |
| G4      | Handle Low Battery in Collection | Manage robot battery during collection phase.                       | FALLBACK(AT5, AT6);  | Achieve    | G2       |
| G5      | Handle Low Battery in Delivery | Manage robot battery during delivery phase.                         | FALLBACK(AT7, AT8);  | Achieve    | G3       |

#### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                    | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location        | Number of Robots |
| ------- | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | --------------- | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage           | Move robot to the storage location.                                  | AND      | Storage         | 1                |
| AT2     | Request Resource              | Send message to storage for resource retrieval.                      | AND      | Storage         | 1                |
| AT3     | Retrieve Resource             | Wait for and retrieve the requested resources.                       | AND      | Storage         | 1                |
| AT4     | Deliver Resource              | Transport resources to the specified location.                       | AND      | Delivery Point  | 1                |
| AT5     | Return to Recharge Station    | Navigate low-battery robot back to recharge station.                 | OR       | Recharge Station| 1                |
| AT6     | Assign Mission to Another Robot | Assign current mission to another robot if battery is low.           | OR       | -               | 1                |
| AT7     | Return to Checkpoint          | Navigate low-battery robot back to checkpoint with resources.        | OR       | Checkpoint      | 1                |
| AT8     | Assign Remaining Task         | Assign remaining delivery task to another robot.                     | OR       | -               | 1                |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**
  - G1 requires both collection and delivery to be completed.

- **G2 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND]**
  - G2 involves navigating to storage, requesting resources, and retrieving them.

- **G3 -> AT4 [AND]**
  - G3 involves delivering the collected resources.

- **G4 -> AT5, AT6 [FALLBACK]**
  - If battery is low during collection, either return to recharge or assign the mission to another robot.

- **G5 -> AT7, AT8 [FALLBACK]**
  - If battery is low during delivery, either return to checkpoint or assign the remaining task to another robot.

This goal model ensures that the mission is executed efficiently, with considerations for battery management and parallel task execution where applicable.
